  "body": "What is owed:\nRotary Offset refuses a face selection by name (the fix for #2848). It cannot keep its roughing ladder to the picked faces.\n\nExpected:\nRotary Offset accepts picked faces of the turned surface. The ladder roughs only over the picked faces. The axis fit still reads the full model.\n\nWhat is known:\n- A clip of the finished path is wrong for a roughing ladder. A kept piece would plunge into stock that the dropped passes did not clear. The cuts along the clip line would be full-width slots.\n- The correct form is a region. `rotary_offset::develop` gives the pocket ladder one rectangle in wrap space (`wrap_rect`). The picked faces must become a region in the same wrap space, and the ladder must run inside it with its own entry law.\n- The seam is the hard part. The wrap mesh is laid two times (one period apart), and the air levels use one lap (`one_lap`). A picked region that crosses the seam must be one piece and must be cut one time.\n\nDone means:\n- Rotary Offset with `SrcRef::Selection` of faces roughs only over the picked faces.\n- A picked region that crosses the seam is cut one time.\n- The entry guards (`plunge_solid::audit_bar`) pass or refuse by name on the bounded ladder.\n- The refusals of `operation::rotary_picks` apply to Rotary Offset.\n- The `not_yet(\"Rotary Offset\")` refusal is removed.\n- Tests pin the bounded ladder, the seam case and the refusals.\n\nFound during the work on #2848.\n",
